{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/423369-strix-blood-bonds","id":423369,"title":"Strix & Blood Bonds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-28T13:23:54-08:00","id":423369,"title":"Strix & Blood Bonds","content":"Greetings!<br /> <br /> The book is clear on Strix being immune to Vitae Addiction and the Vinculum. Fair enough.<br /> <br /> What it does not seem to mention is, whether the host can become Vitae addicted and blood bonded from Vitae ingested by the Strix <i>and </i>what happens when a Strix possessing a host feeds its Vitae to another. Can a Strix create a blood bond and, if yes, is the victim bound to the host or the Strix?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T04:44:23-08:00","id":423987,"title":"","content":"They can't form blood bonds when they're not in a vampire, that's for sure - their host's blood doesn't count as vitae at all. <br /> <br /> In a vampire, that's less clear. I would go out on a limb and say it does, as it would probably blow their cover if it didn't, and it's mentioned that they can make/feed ghouls while possessing a vamp. I would also say the bond applied to the vampire, because they're kind of using them as a filter to get it to work at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T04:51:42-08:00","id":423989,"title":"","content":"I would say that, should the host become vitae-addicted, the strix would continue to act out depending on its nature. It might enjoy driving a body into deprivation, after all. The Vinculum, however, I would rule would just flat out not work on the person. Blood bound strix doesn't sound right to my ears. All else, the way their mind processed the vinculum could be against the vampire's favor. These aren't human beings with human minds.<br /> <br /> If a vampire possesses a vampire and has the vampire bind someone else, its too the vampire itself, not the possessing strix. In my opinion, anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T04:58:13-08:00","id":423993,"title":"","content":"Actually I don't think blood binding the host would be a problem. The host gets a vinculum, and is driven by an unconditional love for the vampire. The strix doesn't care, because the host isn't driving their body. Same with addiction. Strix can easily forget to eat and starve their host to death. They don't give a crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:25:54-08:00","id":424321,"title":"","content":"Just imagine a strix possessing you, getting you blood bound, using your body to ruin the domitor's life so she hates you, and then leaving you holding the bag. Ouch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:17:47-08:00","id":424358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/423369-strix-blood-bonds?p=424321#post424321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just imagine a strix possessing you, getting you blood bound, using your body to ruin the domitor's life so she hates you, and then leaving you holding the bag. Ouch.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely the kind of thing I could see a Strix doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:01:27-08:00","id":424675,"title":"","content":"I think if Synthesis is used then the host's blood works like a normal vampire. Excluding that, vitae can only be given when the host is a vampire. I don't think it can do anything except feed a ghoul, but if allowing the vitae to create addiction and vinculum, I would give it to the host. The strix would gain the benefits while possessing the host. I think since the vitae/blood taken by a strix is transmuted by the strix the host is also immune to blood addiction and vinculum while possessed. They seem more psychological than physical so I think that it would work just like breaking points (don't count against the host). Diablerie has a physical component so that is different. I'm not seeing a down side to allowing these things, but it would make the strix even scarier to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T02:17:33-08:00","id":424976,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Synthesis just turn the host <i>into</i> a normal vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:57:31-08:00","id":425367,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Synthesis turns the host into a vampire.<br /> <br /> I'd say that blood given by a possessed vampire forms a blood bond with the host body, not the Stryx inside. The way I conceptualize this is that when the Stryx enters the body, it absorbs the vitae inside the vampire into itself. When it needs to spend the blood to do something, such as activating a discipline or using the blush of life, it pumps that vitae back into the body to do so. Since the blood would then come from the body of the vampire in question, it would be the beneficiary of the blood bond. <br /> <br /> When inside a host, unless the possessor has Breath Eater, the rules suggest that the host in question must feed only through the resources it would actually have to feed with. So, that suggests that vampires are latching on with fangs and sucking up blood the old fashioned way. Since the Stryx then steals the blood from the host, the way I see it that blood does enter the host first, and thus the host can be blood bonded as normal. I offer up as precident for the host changing due to Stryx actions the diablerie consequences. A vampire that has no idea it did the deed still loses humanity and reaps the rewards for amaranth committed while possessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1744-thantrax","name":"Thantrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:05:03-08:00","id":425746,"title":"","content":"Synthesis turns the host into a Stryxpire or whatever you want to call it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was never clear what exactly occurs with Synthesis, but the example has a Stryx that can Embrace. It isn't clear whether the unusually strong bond is normal Synthesis or it is an unusually strong Synthesis, but normal Stryx in host bodies can't embrace.<br /> <br /> I see diablerie consequences and lack of breaking points as evidence the host is immune. Breaking points are purely mental. Blood addiction and bond seem completely mental as well. Diablerie imparts a physical, and mental, change. The soul sucking changed the host. The blood/vitae belongs to the Stryx. The host only gets some of what the Stryx is unable to take with it.<br /> <br /> You can decide it either way, but I don't think there is great justification no matter what you decide. Go with your preference knowing that if the host is affected then you have a lot more record keeping than if it is not. A Stryx <i>will</i> take any vitae offered like a blood addict would. It isn't like there is any downside for the Stryx.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:24:21-08:00","id":425757,"title":"","content":"I think that one was done via the Preservation dread power, which can turn a host into a pseudo-vampire while the strix is in it. Plus a bunch of weird powers on top, because the list they gave you isn't supposed to be exhaustive. <br /> <br /> Speaking of, can a strix in a non-vampire host commit diablerie? They seem to have all the necessary components in some fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T23:23:33-08:00","id":426239,"title":"","content":"Not unless you include revenants as non-vampire hosts.<br /> <br /> &quot;A Strix gains one dot of Shadow Potency every 100 years,<br /> and may only additionally increase it through diablerie \u2014 either<br /> by possessing a vampire who commits Amaranth on another<br /> vampire, or by feeding from and diablerizing another Strix<br /> when in Shadow Form.&quot;<br /> <br /> As Possess Revenant includes diablerie, the writers would not.<br /> <br /> The Baron was a vampire before the Stryx came along. The Baron Stryx has Synthesis. I think he is the only example that Synthesis could have been used on the host. The others don't have a specific host or aren't vampires. Not at all clear what happens to a host that survives Synthesis, but the others become vampires if not already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 03-03-2015, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T02:06:19-08:00","id":426331,"title":"","content":"The baron is weird because it seems to have the strix using synthesis to do a thing that synthesis doesn't actually do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}